# This repository publishes the built dashboard and the three CSVs it reads,
# served by GitHub Pages. Everything else in this folder stays out of version
# control -- the source workbook (its Validation_Log holds internal QA notes),
# the Power BI project, the brand guidelines PDF, and the saved copy of the
# irena.org page.
#
# So: exclude everything, then re-admit only what is published. Git will not
# descend into an excluded directory, which is why each directory on the path
# is un-ignored before its contents are re-ignored.
#
# The CSVs are published because the dashboard fetches them from its own folder;
# without them the preview would render its "no data files were found" notice and
# look broken. They disclose nothing new -- the same data is already inlined in
# the published HTML as the offline fallback. NOT published: data.json,
# artifact-body.html, EMBED-INSTRUCTIONS.md, width-test.html and all of src/.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/index.html

!/webdash/
/webdash/*
!/webdash/dist/
/webdash/dist/*
!/webdash/dist/national-energy-planning-dashboard.html
!/webdash/dist/Documents.csv
!/webdash/dist/Doc_Tools.csv
!/webdash/dist/MT_Key.csv

# Power BI local artefacts, kept from the previous .gitignore. Redundant under
# the rules above, but harmless and correct if the scope ever widens.
**/.pbi/localSettings.json
**/.pbi/cache.abf
